Given:
A binary tree
Two nodes P and Q

Find the lowest (deepest) node that has both P and Q as descendants.

A node can also be a descendant of itself.

Example 1
              3
            /   \
           5     1
         /  \   / \
        6    2 0   8
            / \
           7   4

Find the LCA of P = 5, Q = 1

Answer 3

-----------------------------

public static TreeNode lowestCommanAncestor(TreeNode root, TreeNode p, TreeNode q){
    if(root == null || root == p || root == q){
        return root;
    }
    
    TreeNode left = lowestCommanAncestor(root.left, p, q);
    TreeNode right = lowestCommanAncestor(root.right, p, q);
    
    if(left != null && right != null){
        return root;
    } 
    
    if(left != null){
        return right;
    }
    
     if(right != null){
        return left;
    }

return null;

}
